message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PermaCycle v1.0.1: A Coupled Hydro–Thermal–Geochemical Model for Permafrost Dynamics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: You
    given-names: Kehua
    affiliation: "University of Texas at Austin"
    email: "kehua@ig.utexas.edu"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0194-8720"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-05-05"
abstract: "PermaCycle is a one-dimensional MATLAB-based numerical model for simulating the evolution of subsea permafrost and methane hydrate stability along Arctic continental shelves over glacial-interglacial cycles. The model couples hydrological, thermal, and geochemical processes, including fluid flow, heat transport, salt transport, ice formation and melting, and methane hydrate stability calculations."
keywords:
  - permafrost
  - subsea permafrost
  - methane hydrate
  - Arctic continental shelf
  - Glacial-interglacial cycle
  - hydrothermal modeling
  - geochemical transport
  - MATLAB
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KehuaYou/PermaCycle"
